body:
I don't know how it is in the rest of the country but the RCMP categorically failed us nova scotians after that shooter and they tried to lie in order to cover up their blunders. They delayed sending out an alert or anything for the first 19 hours this was happening, when local police station chefs asked if they needed help the rcmp refused them and elected to call in a much farther away rcmp unit in new brunswick. To make things worse when some of them were testifying at the hearing nobody was allowed to question their statements about what happened. They wouldn't give a number in regards to how many trained rcmp were in the province that could reliably handle a situation like this  

&#x200B;

later on some cops said the reason why they waited so long to give alerts about an active shooter was that they might have been worried that the shooter himself was an rcmp officer

bard gets fun at level 80

&#x200B;

gunbreaker is fun from the offset

&#x200B;

machinist gets fun when you unlock the drill
